# OAuth Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your client IDs
# 
# IMPORTANT: These OAuth apps must be configured with the following redirect URI:
#   - Development: http://localhost:5173/auth/callback
#   - Production: https://your-domain.com/auth/callback
#
# Without these client IDs configured, users will only be able to use Guest Mode.

# Microsoft OAuth (Azure AD)
# ============================
# 1. Go to: https://portal.azure.com/#blade/Microsoft_AAD_RegisteredApps/ApplicationsListBlade
# 2. Click "New registration"
# 3. Name: "Story Presentation App" (or your preferred name)
# 4. Supported account types: "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts"
# 5. Redirect URI: Select "Single-page application (SPA)" and enter your callback URL
# 6. After creation, copy the "Application (client) ID"
#
# Required API Permissions (add under "API permissions"):
#   - Microsoft Graph: openid, profile, email, User.Read, Files.ReadWrite
VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=your-microsoft-client-id-here

# Google OAuth
# ============================
# 1. Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# 2. Create a new project or select existing
# 3. Click "Create Credentials" > "OAuth client ID"
# 4. Application type: "Web application"
# 5. Authorized JavaScript origins: Add your domain (e.g., http://localhost:5173)
# 6. Authorized redirect URIs: Add your callback URL (e.g., http://localhost:5173/auth/callback)
# 7. Copy the "Client ID"
#
# Required OAuth Scopes (configured in code):
#   - openid, profile, email, https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id-here

# Azure SignalR (for real-time collaboration features)
# Optional - collaboration features work without this in local development
# VITE_SIGNALR_CONNECTION_STRING=your-signalr-connection-string-here
